    <statement><p>Evaluate exactly, using the Fundamental Theorem of Calculus:</p>
<p><m>\int_0^{b} 6 e^x dx =</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>6\mathopen{}\left(e^{b}-1\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>e^x</m> is <m>e^x</m>, so an antiderivative of <m>6 e^x</m>
is <m>6 e^x</m>, and we get 
<me>\int_0^{b} 6 e^x dx = 6 e^x\big|_0^{b} = 6 e^{b} - 6 e^0 = 
  6 e^{b} - 6.</me>



</solution>
